1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,077
The fourth arc closed with a contract and a conference.

2
00:00:03,077 --> 00:00:17,325
The overall theme was “the opening of the year”, and the executive from the central company arrived with a conventional bid and an extraordinary recommendation: hire the founder, not the contractor.

3
00:00:17,325 --> 00:00:23,690
The police were at the door, and the offer came with a white envelope.

4
00:00:23,690 --> 00:00:34,014
The agreement had a loophole: a contractor could leave after one visit, and the placement of the mining permit was left to the general office.

5
00:00:34,014 --> 00:00:39,894
“We always know the best position and never the price,” the attendant said.

6
00:00:39,894 --> 00:00:47,659
The petrol bill, the processor, and the specification for the jeans were all in the annex.

7
00:00:47,659 --> 00:00:52,793
In the evening they joined the police and the company at a memorial dinner.

8
00:00:52,793 --> 00:00:59,758
“It is possible to spend a week on a white memorial and a pound on a plug,” Maya said.

9
00:00:59,758 --> 00:01:11,302
“The functional part is the part nobody photographs.” A contraction of the budget followed, and the design of the balcony had to be redone.

10
00:01:11,302 --> 00:01:17,467
The shift in the market was indeed a cause of the closure, but not the only one.

11
00:01:17,467 --> 00:01:26,586
“A lot of small engagements are one engagement,” the executive said, and the room noticed the white sheet under the forge.

12
00:01:26,586 --> 00:01:33,481
The forge, the garden, and the night shift were all that remained of the older plan.

13
00:01:33,481 --> 00:01:40,506
They created a small notice, an ad, and an explanation of the estimate in three languages.

14
00:01:40,506 --> 00:01:47,105
The acceptance of the offer, when it came, was shorter than the offer itself.

15
00:01:47,105 --> 00:01:51,275
“Tell them we are not a department,” she said.

16
00:01:51,275 --> 00:01:56,480
“We are a position, a detail, and a year of work.”

17
00:01:56,480 --> 00:02:00,155
The general office wrote back within a week.

18
00:02:00,155 --> 00:02:10,259
It accepted the contract, ignored the loophole, and sent a second attendant to the balcony with a functional plug and a printed estimate.

19
00:02:10,259 --> 00:02:15,424
“A conventional bid is a promise in a suit,” the founder said.

20
00:02:15,424 --> 00:02:30,318
“An extraordinary one is a promise in jeans.” They spent the last of the month on petrol and a processor, and told the police exactly what they had spent and why the loophole mattered to a public contract.

21
00:02:30,318 --> 00:02:38,836
The deadline had been met; what it had cost them was the belief that a deadline is the hard part.
